Dear all,

Following yesterday's Board meeting (24 October) here is the Q3 note, a few days ahead of the call. Everything below is unaudited management information and is subject to the usual close adjustments, so please do not quote it outside your own organisations.

THE QUARTER IN FIVE LINES

- Revenue EUR 29.5m in Q3 (Q3 2023: EUR 25.5m), +15.7% year on year. Nine months: EUR 84.4m.
- EBITDA EUR 5.9m, a margin of 20.0%. Nine months: EUR 15.7m (18.6%).
- Net debt EUR 57.5m at 30 September; net debt / LTM EBITDA 2.74x against the 3.50x covenant ceiling; interest cover 6.3x against a floor of 4.0x.
- Cash EUR 9.7m plus EUR 8.0m undrawn on the revolving facility, so liquidity of EUR 17.7m.
- Headcount 327 FTE.

Pharma Lanes and Monitoring & Software did most of the work, again. The two new Helvetia lanes out of Hamburg-Waltershof have been live since 1 August and are included in the numbers above and in the guidance below. Reefer Services grew 11.0%, with container-days up 8.4%.

GUIDANCE: RAISED

In April (annual report) we said revenue of EUR 104m to 108m and EBITDA of EUR 19.0m to 20.0m for 2024. That guidance is withdrawn and replaced with:

- Revenue: EUR 112m to EUR 115m (our own forecast is EUR 113.8m)
- EBITDA: EUR 21.0m to EUR 22.0m (forecast EUR 21.5m, a margin of 18.9%)
- Capex: about EUR 16.9m, down from the EUR 19.5m budget, mostly timing as Thermaglide deliveries slip into 2025
- Net debt / EBITDA at 31 December: around 2.6x (previously "below 3.0x")

The range assumes normal citrus volumes in Q4. It does not assume any outcome of the Oakhaven mediation beyond the provision already booked.

BOARD DECISIONS OF 24 OCTOBER

1. Phase 2 of the plug racks at Rotterdam-Maasvlakte (120 more points, EUR 2.35m) approved, to be tendered with three bids.
2. The CFO is authorised to sign the amendment that moves the maturity of the EUR 15.0m revolving credit facility from 31 October 2026 to 31 October 2027. The fee is 0.35% of the commitment, EUR 52,500. Jonas, I will send the formal request letter on Monday 28 October with the Q3 compliance package; the compliance certificate itself follows by 15 November.
3. The Board noted FY2025 budget v3 (revenue EUR 126.4m, EBITDA EUR 24.8m). It is a working basis only. Final adoption is on 12 December.

THE CALL

Q3 investor call: Thursday 7 November 2024, 15:00 CET, 45 minutes. Teams link in the calendar invitation; if Teams misbehaves (it usually does around 15:02) the backup dial-in is +48 58 555 0143, PIN 417 902.

Best,
Priya

